      "role": "user",
      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>I see what you mean about the \"rigor\" angle, but I'm a bit worried. If we spend the whole section explaining why we *failed* to hit our targets, it's just going to draw more attention to the fact that we missed the mark by 15%. It might make us look like we're making excuses.\n\nIs there a way we can frame the 5% result differently? Like, can we present it in a way that emphasizes the success and the scale of the achievement rather than the deficit? I really need us to come across as a powerhouse that delivers results.",
