      "content": "That's getting closer, but even with that spin, \"5%\" still looks small on paper. I'm looking at some of the other successful applicants from last year, and they're all reporting massive, double-digit jumps. \n\nIf we want to be competitive for $5M, we need to sound like we're already seeing the kind of transformative results they're looking for. Can we use stronger language? Maybe something that characterizes the 5% as a \"significant breakthrough\" or a \"transformative leap\" in coral recovery? I just need to know how to bridge that gap between reality and what a funder needs to see to write a check.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
